  "aiContextParagraph": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi has engaged in a range of diplomatic and domestic activities this week. Domestically, the Prime Minister observed Constitution Day, emphasizing efforts to strengthen public connection with the nation's foundational legal framework. Internationally, he held discussions with German Chancellor Friedrich Merz regarding the finalization of a free trade pact between India and the European Union, which officials believe will create significant new economic opportunities. Additionally, India’s pavilion at the Venice Biennale received the Visitors’ Lion award, an achievement the Prime Minister described as a source of national pride. In the administrative sphere, the Prime Minister has directed ministers to remain prepared for an upcoming parliamentary session expected before mid-December. Policy discussions also focused on domestic economic issues, including the integration of vocational training with specific industry demands to enhance local employment prospects.",
